  "response": "Confirmed the key premises by reading the source. Here's the review.\n\n## Headline\n\n**Nothing in this PR trips a standard gate.** `summary.high: 0`; the ceiling is `severity: medium` (0.55) and the ceiling on `agent_risk` is 0.45. `crimes scan --changed --fail-on high` exits 0 on this diff.\n\nBut the count is misleading in a way worth stating before the triage: **46 of 99 findings (46%) are the repo's layout, not its code.** This is `vercel/next-learn` — every path pairs a `final-example` against a `starter-example`, ten `basics/*` step snapshots against each other, and `seo/` against `seo/demo/`. I checked all 46 `exact_duplicate_block` findings: **every one spans a variant boundary.** None are duplication *within* an app. Collapsing variant mirrors across all detectors, 99 findings reduce to ~31 distinct code-level issues.\n\n**Triage rule I applied:** *block* if the change lets two places answer the same domain question differently; *warn* if it's real but local and creates no second source of truth; *ignore* if the finding is true about the repo layout or the detector's assumptions rather than the code.\n\n---\n\n## BLOCK MERGE — 2 findings, 1 defect\n\n### `duplicated_role_status_plan_check` — `crime_00072`, `crime_00073`\n`severity: medium (0.55)` · `confidence: 0.70` · **`agent_risk: 0.22`**\n\nI'm blocking against the score, and here's why. The scan reports these as the *joint-lowest* agent_risk of any medium finding. Reading the code inverts that:\n\n- `app/lib/actions.ts:20` already declares the source of truth: `status: z.enum(['pending', 'paid'], {...})`.\n- `app/ui/invoices/status.tsx:4` takes `{ status }: { status: string }` — **typed `string`, not the enum** — then compares raw literals at L10, L11, L15, L21.\n- `app/ui/invoices/edit-form.tsx:108,124` does its own `invoice.status === \"pending\"` / `=== \"paid\"`.\n- All of it exists twice more in `starter-example`.\n\nThe canonical definition exists and is bypassed by every consumer, with the type system opted out. Adding an `'overdue'` status means four coordinated edits across two apps, and nothing fails if you miss one — the badge silently renders empty (both ternaries fall to `null`). That is precisely the \"multiple sources of truth\" failure `agent_risk` exists to catch.\n\n**Why the score under-reads it:** `blast_radius: 0` (leaf UI files, no importers) drags the aggregate down. Blast radius is the wrong axis for a policy that is *replicated* rather than *imported* — copies have no import edges by construction. Fix: `export type InvoiceStatus = z.infer<...>['status']` from `actions.ts`, narrow the `status.tsx` prop to it, and the compiler enforces the rest.\n\n---\n\n## WARN — 10 findings\n\n| # | Detector | sev / agent_risk | Call |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `00006` | `magic_domain_literal_scatter` | 0.50 / **0.41** | Warn, not block — see below |\n| `00020` | `direct_date` | 0.35 / 0.28 | Real testability gap in a write path |\n| `00071` | `duplicate_component_shape` | 0.55 / 0.22 | Only duplication finding that isn't a variant mirror |\n| `00013`,`00014`,`00015` | `commented_out_code` | 0.25 / 0.39 | Dead code in the *finished* app |\n| `00031`,`00032` | `deep_import` | 0.35 / 0.24 | Fragile but unavoidable |\n| `00095`,`00096` | `oversized_raster` | 0.40 / 0.14 | 487 KB LCP image |\n\n**`crime_00006` (`\"status\"`, agent_risk 0.41 — the report's #2)** — downgrade. `actions.ts:43` is `formData.get('status')`, a FormData key that *must* match `name=\"status\"` on the form inputs (`create-form.tsx:97`). That coupling is a framework contract, not duplicated policy, and the values are already pinned by the `z.enum` 23 lines above. Real coupling, low hazard.\n\n**`crime_00020`** — `actions.ts:57`: `const date = new Date().toISOString().split('T')[0]`, written straight into the invoice row. The evidence correctly notes *\"none decide a branch\"* — it records rather than gates, so severity stays low. But it makes `createInvoice` untestable without freezing the clock. Small fix, worth doing.\n\n**`crime_00071`** — the one duplication finding that isn't variant noise: `create-form.tsx:142-150` ↔ `edit-form.tsx:152-160` are two files in the **same** app (and again in starter). The shared subtree is the Cancel/Submit button row. Genuine extraction win.\n\n**`crime_00013`/`00014`/`00015`** — `data.ts:19-20` and `final-example/app/query/route.ts:17-20`. The `route.ts` one is interesting: it's the *inverse* of the starter file — the finished app has the placeholder response commented out and the real implementation live. Leftover scaffolding in the shipped app. 4 lines, delete it.\n\n**`crime_00031`/`00032`** — `react-syntax-highlighter/dist/cjs/styles/prism` is genuinely unpublished surface that breaks on repackaging, but it's the import path that package's own README documents. Nothing to fix; pin the dependency major.\n\n**`crime_00095`/`00096`** — 487 KB `hero-desktop.png`, one distinct asset counted twice. This is the LCP image on the landing page; `next/image` optimises delivery but not the bytes committed to the repo. The only asset finding with a real user-facing cost.\n\n---\n\n## IGNORE — 87 findings\n\n### `exact_duplicate_block` — 46 findings · `severity: medium (0.55)` · `agent_risk: 0.22–0.25`\nAll 46 pair across sibling tutorial variants. The suggested fix — \"extract the duplicated block into a shared helper\" — would destroy the exact property the repo exists to demonstrate. High confidence (0.95) and correctly medium severity, but this is a **scope-class** mismatch: the detector has no concept of \"sibling example directories are independent roots.\"\n\n### `raster_should_be_vector` — 12 findings · `0.35 / 0.16`\nClean false-positive class. Every one is `public/customers/*.png` at 56×56 or 60×60 — **photographs of people**, not icons. The detector keys on dimensions alone; a portrait cannot become an SVG. Lowest agent_risk in the report and it's right about that, just wrong about the premise.\n\n### `sync_io_in_hotpath` — 6 findings · `0.40 / **0.45** — the report's highest agent_risk`\nIgnoring the top-scoring finding class, on evidence. `basics/basics-final/pages/index.js:39` is `export async function getStaticProps()` calling `getSortedPostsData()`; `getAllPostIds` feeds `getStaticPaths`. These are Next.js **build-time** data helpers — the summary's *\"each invocation blocks the event loop\"* doesn't apply, because there is no request-time invocation. Reading markdown synchronously in a build script is the correct implementation. The detector's `tier: domain` classification can't see the Next.js call-site contract, and all six are the same file copied across `basics/*` steps.\n\n### `design_token_escape` — 8 findings · `0.40 / 0.22`\nFour distinct files, doubled. The \"hard-coded style values\" are Tailwind arbitrary values: `h-[18px] w-[18px]` on heroicons (`create-form.tsx:44,73`) and `px-[14px]` (L92). Icon sizing beside Tailwind utilities, in a project with no design-token layer to escape from. The detector presumes a design system exists.\n\n### `commented_out_code` in `starter-example` — 7 findings · `0.25–0.45 / 0.37–0.39`\nDeliberate, self-documenting tutorial scaffolding. `latest-invoices.tsx:17` reads `{/* NOTE: Uncomment this code in Chapter 7 */}`; `query/route.ts:19` reads `'Uncomment this file and remove this line.'` The detector's stated risk — *\"mislead humans and agents into copying or reviving stale behaviour\"* — is exactly inverted here: reviving it **is** the intent. These carry the highest agent_risk outside `sync_io`, and it's wrong in every case.\n\n### `direct_date` in `utils.ts` — 2 findings · `0.35 / 0.30`\n`utils.ts:14` is `new Date(dateStr)` inside `formatDateToLocal(dateStr: string)` — an argument is passed, so it's fully deterministic. The detector counts the constructor without checking arity. False positive (contrast `crime_00020`, which is argument-free and warned above).\n\n### `singular_plural_type_mismatch` — 2 findings · `0.30 / 0.28`\n`generateYAxis(revenue: Revenue[])`. \"Revenue\" is a mass noun; \"revenues\" would be worse. The finding names its own escape hatch — this is what `allowedNames` is for.\n\n### `oversized_raster` (4 of 6) · `0.40 / 0.14`\n`opengraph-image.png` at 237 KB is normal for an OG card and never on the critical path. `seo/public/large-image.jpg` at 422 KB is *named* large-image and is the subject of the SEO tutorial chapter — it's the demo.\n\n---\n\n## Where the scores and the risk disagree\n\nThe two most useful signals in this report are inverted relative to actual hazard:\n\n| | agent_risk | Actual |\n|---|---|---|\n| `sync_io_in_hotpath` | **0.45** (highest) | Build-time helper — no hazard |\n| `magic_domain_literal_scatter` \"status\" | **0.41** | Framework-enforced FormData key |\n| `commented_out_code` (starter) | **0.39** | Scaffolding you're *meant* to uncomment |\n| `duplicated_role_status_plan_check` | **0.22** (joint-lowest medium) | **The one blocker** |\n\nCommon cause: three of the four inflated scores carry `test_gap: 0.5` and `blast_radius` from importer counts, while the genuine policy duplication scores `blast_radius: 0` because replicated code has no import edges. Worth a calibration look — replication and coupling are different shapes of blast radius, and the current formula only measures the second.\n\n## Actions\n\n1. **Block on `crime_00072`/`00073`** — export the `z.enum` type, narrow `InvoiceStatus`'s prop from `string`.\n2. **Add a `crimes.config.json`** treating `dashboard/*`, `basics/*`, `seo`/`seo/demo` as independent roots — that alone removes 46 findings, and every remaining variant mirror across the other detectors.\n3. **File four false-positive verdicts** so they don't recur:\n   ```\n   crimes feedback raster_should_be_vector::dashboard/final-example/public/customers/amy-burns.png:: \\\n     --verdict fp --note \"Customer avatar photographs, not icons — SVG is not a possible target format\"\n   crimes feedback sync_io_in_hotpath::basics/basics-final/lib/posts.js:: \\\n     --verdict fp --note \"getStaticProps/getStaticPaths data helpers — build-time, never on a request path\"\n   crimes feedback direct_date::dashboard/final-example/app/lib/utils.ts:: \\\n     --verdict fp --note \"new Date(dateStr) takes an argument — deterministic, not a clock read\"\n   crimes feedback commented_out_code::dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/dashboard/latest-invoices.tsx::::7f5844254e42 \\\n     --verdict fp --note \"Tutorial scaffolding — the comment instructs the reader to uncomment it in Chapter 7\"\n   ```\n   And add `revenue` to `detectors.options.singular_plural_type_mismatch.allowedNames`.\n4. **Warn-only on the other 10** — none justify holding the merge.",
